modules.details_md:
The package has no code of its own; its docstring is the map of the simulator:

- `world.py` simulates the game on a real map;
- `fakes.py` puts it behind the seams gamelab already has (`Eyes`, `gamelab.control.client`, time);
- `scenarios.py` runs gamelab's entry points on it;
- `golden.py` records their traces and checks the code still does the same (`python -m gamelab.sim.golden record|check`).

Its safety promise: nothing here sends a key to the game or writes under `gamelab/lab` during a run. The stack runs only inside `with scenarios.Sim(model, scenario) as sim:`, where the fakes are in place, and opening any file under `gamelab/lab` for writing raises `SimViolation`. One exception is spelled out: a telemetry file opened *before* the run (as `python -m gamelab sim` does) keeps receiving records, so the mini-map can show the run.
